{
  "cardiac-arrest-als": {
    "durationMs": 104599,
    "audio": "explainers/cardiac-arrest-als.m4a",
    "scenes": [
      {
        "id": "title",
        "startMs": 600,
        "endMs": 6155,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Adult cardiac arrest.",
            "startMs": 600,
            "endMs": 2260
          },
          {
            "text": "The advanced life support approach, in under two minutes.",
            "startMs": 2510,
            "endMs": 6155
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "862d78912c7ef47d155b4f1e5b0fa7c2c674e64d2dc959715ec7a3b042daab86"
      },
      {
        "id": "start-cpr",
        "startMs": 6855,
        "endMs": 23468,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "If the patient is unresponsive and not breathing normally, start chest compressions at once.",
            "startMs": 6855,
            "endMs": 12776
          },
          {
            "text": "Thirty compressions to two breaths, five to six centimetres deep, one hundred to one hundred and twenty per minute.",
            "startMs": 13026,
            "endMs": 19585
          },
          {
            "text": "Attach the defibrillator and call the resuscitation team.",
            "startMs": 19835,
            "endMs": 23468
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "1d5ed53064f2394a5e493e5de76dfd5fbabaae6b66f5c4401f6392bb2317407c"
      },
      {
        "id": "rhythm-check",
        "startMs": 24168,
        "endMs": 29015,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Pause compressions for less than five seconds to assess the rhythm.",
            "startMs": 24168,
            "endMs": 27813
          },
          {
            "text": "Is it shockable?",
            "startMs": 28063,
            "endMs": 29015
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "7ac829ff3a40c1e68059ae98191d903a03aefc453e7e459844fe6d17871a514a"
      },
      {
        "id": "shockable",
        "startMs": 29715,
        "endMs": 38120,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Ventricular fibrillation or pulseless V T: give one shock, then resume compressions immediately, for two minutes.",
            "startMs": 29715,
            "endMs": 38120
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "583ae9d9be4d31892e179da0eb8716c687cc1743b7ef3ef1b63a2a6cc4c8b7b6"
      },
      {
        "id": "shockable-drugs",
        "startMs": 38820,
        "endMs": 52717,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "After the third shock, give adrenaline one milligram and amiodarone three hundred milligrams.",
            "startMs": 38820,
            "endMs": 44648
          },
          {
            "text": "Repeat adrenaline every three to five minutes.",
            "startMs": 44898,
            "endMs": 47870
          },
          {
            "text": "After the fifth shock, give amiodarone one hundred and fifty milligrams.",
            "startMs": 48120,
            "endMs": 52717
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "c7939893c33b1b204570104384a75118dc81f552d43b4f2c8fa4c70733127493"
      },
      {
        "id": "non-shockable",
        "startMs": 53417,
        "endMs": 62849,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "For P E A or asystole, give adrenaline one milligram as soon as possible.",
            "startMs": 53417,
            "endMs": 58246
          },
          {
            "text": "Continue C P R, and reassess the rhythm every two minutes.",
            "startMs": 58496,
            "endMs": 62849
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "5b80e7ba2c7f2a88d4d64987118ed0c7fb3f5f1c656dbe3ecde15aa517fd04c0"
      },
      {
        "id": "reversible-causes",
        "startMs": 63549,
        "endMs": 79581,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Throughout the arrest, look for reversible causes: the four H's and four T's.",
            "startMs": 63549,
            "endMs": 69330
          },
          {
            "text": "Hypoxia, hypovolaemia, potassium and metabolic disorders, and temperature.",
            "startMs": 69580,
            "endMs": 75303
          },
          {
            "text": "Thrombosis, tamponade, toxins, and tension pneumothorax.",
            "startMs": 75553,
            "endMs": 79581
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "59e8580725dbb3144278b1af74ae290e4a6144f965ffbfcdaea14f9227259e20"
      },
      {
        "id": "rosc",
        "startMs": 80281,
        "endMs": 94381,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "If circulation returns, move straight to post resuscitation care.",
            "startMs": 80281,
            "endMs": 84774
          },
          {
            "text": "Titrate oxygen to a saturation of ninety four to ninety eight percent, record a twelve lead E C G, and avoid low blood pressure.",
            "startMs": 85024,
            "endMs": 94381
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "9f45e75013d40d3f78121c6261c00ed121c9fc83a3938c496cd7d2ca98040bec"
      },
      {
        "id": "outro",
        "startMs": 95081,
        "endMs": 103399,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "This summary follows the E R C twenty twenty five guidelines.",
            "startMs": 95081,
            "endMs": 99713
          },
          {
            "text": "Always follow the physician's orders and your local protocol.",
            "startMs": 99963,
            "endMs": 103399
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "6517238b2460b35f1b37066caf4f2bd0f16c5200088ecfc5462fa827702fcd65"
      }
    ]
  },
  "mechanism-adrenaline": {
    "durationMs": 37913,
    "audio": "explainers/mechanism-adrenaline.m4a",
    "scenes": [
      {
        "id": "title",
        "startMs": 600,
        "endMs": 4240,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Adrenaline in cardiac arrest.",
            "startMs": 600,
            "endMs": 2771
          },
          {
            "text": "How does it work?",
            "startMs": 3021,
            "endMs": 4240
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "b28a947ff7b54537116d95b4ce6c7a0211661e6ede7c9f1ca1712bd07c14d5be"
      },
      {
        "id": "alpha",
        "startMs": 4940,
        "endMs": 11853,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Adrenaline stimulates alpha one receptors on the smooth muscle of blood vessels.",
            "startMs": 4940,
            "endMs": 10152
          },
          {
            "text": "The vessels constrict.",
            "startMs": 10402,
            "endMs": 11853
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "a84b5df65d539d3fa14d4d042082267ca1fc6f6ea7f21e0ffd10457e8795f715"
      },
      {
        "id": "perfusion",
        "startMs": 12553,
        "endMs": 20169,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Constriction raises the pressure in the aorta between compressions, which pushes more blood into the coronary and brain arteries.",
            "startMs": 12553,
            "endMs": 20169
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "ddc14cbc99d09a493bd75ff6232b839f1f4560108029300d6b2253268db0598f"
      },
      {
        "id": "restart",
        "startMs": 20869,
        "endMs": 26128,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Better blood flow to the heart muscle increases the chance that a normal rhythm returns.",
            "startMs": 20869,
            "endMs": 26128
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "430e53ed1654e065b1c340be6d1f2ec01b0ff481e6d51052cfee3d1eb36f94c3"
      },
      {
        "id": "beta",
        "startMs": 26828,
        "endMs": 36713,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Its beta effects make the heart beat faster and harder.",
            "startMs": 26828,
            "endMs": 30310
          },
          {
            "text": "That helps after a pulse returns, but it also increases the heart's oxygen demand.",
            "startMs": 30560,
            "endMs": 36713
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "84b0086c5a928e0bb7b866bdbc79d84d1d586bf6237573888957dfbe771ae13b"
      }
    ]
  },
  "mechanism-amiodarone": {
    "durationMs": 38457,
    "audio": "explainers/mechanism-amiodarone.m4a",
    "scenes": [
      {
        "id": "title",
        "startMs": 600,
        "endMs": 2973,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Amiodarone.",
            "startMs": 600,
            "endMs": 1528
          },
          {
            "text": "How does it work?",
            "startMs": 1778,
            "endMs": 2973
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "182db06564a5ce2832866815e44b8afc40963b757cb9864d4b8c983b9c494df2"
      },
      {
        "id": "action-potential",
        "startMs": 3673,
        "endMs": 12183,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Each heart cell fires with a wave of electrical charge, called the action potential, and then needs time to recover before it can fire again.",
            "startMs": 3673,
            "endMs": 12183
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "b60842ed7b435037f5d8c7b3d281d3860012666126caffe7debde22736f807e1"
      },
      {
        "id": "potassium-block",
        "startMs": 12883,
        "endMs": 20655,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Amiodarone mainly blocks potassium channels.",
            "startMs": 12883,
            "endMs": 15878
          },
          {
            "text": "Recovery is slower, so each cell stays refractory for longer.",
            "startMs": 16128,
            "endMs": 20655
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "e3d97c783f27331b784ba77b6febd7b7fd0a2ee0161197fa819c8fac1622c094"
      },
      {
        "id": "other-channels",
        "startMs": 21355,
        "endMs": 25882,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "It also blocks sodium and calcium channels, and beta receptors.",
            "startMs": 21355,
            "endMs": 25882
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "00108dd0f662c91bd5ffe6ffa72b816dbff2933db30903e1157c608eb01e002c"
      },
      {
        "id": "vf",
        "startMs": 26582,
        "endMs": 37257,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "A longer refractory period makes it harder for chaotic circuits, like ventricular fibrillation, to keep going.",
            "startMs": 26582,
            "endMs": 33884
          },
          {
            "text": "So the next shock is more likely to succeed.",
            "startMs": 34134,
            "endMs": 37257
          }
        ],
        "textSha256": "7be6e9c2e00bff240ae3add0d57c11fc4284141869328cdb5dc463f1b8fd3db8"
      }
    ]
  }
}
